<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Bancomext plans two bln pesos in Q2 loans.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Bancomext plans two bln pesos in Q2 loans.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's foreign trade bank (Bancomext) said it intended to increase the amount of loans it will grant during the second quarter of 1997 to two billion pesos, the bank's director general said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;In the second quarter we will maybe reach a level of some two billion (pesos) and grow from then onwards,&quot; Bancomext Director General Enrique Vilatela told reporters.</p>
<p>Bancomext granted a total of one billion pesos in loans during the first quarter of the year, and its financing budget for 1997 totals 10 billion pesos.</p>
<p>((--Veronica Galan, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9552))</p>
